{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"biggish-allied-aruanas","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/unit cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_create_duplicate_warning.py:1-13` — Preserve normalized-title recency signal, per-surface channel, advisory posture, and disabled/corrupt controls. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_criteria_overlay.py:376-380, 410-415` — Preserve malformed-`applies_to` fail-closed behavior and explicit `[\"**\"]` compatibility edge. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_criteria_snapshot.py:1-14, 138-140, 142-145, 204-208` — Preserve immutable effective-policy snapshot and empty-changes applicability distinctions. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_criteria_vocabulary_reviewers.py:1-16` — Preserve vocabulary consolidation and explicitly distinct experimental/DoD meanings. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_criterion_effectiveness.py:1-10` — Preserve reproducible metrics, extraction/math, auto-inclusion, and nontrivial corpus check. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_criterion_preview.py:1-15, 301-306` — Preserve LLM/DET preview outcomes, unsupported modes, timeout posture, atomic authoring, and sanitized dotted-id path. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_cross_session_warn_routes.py:1-10, 20-23` — Preserve route-derived policy set and exact intentional policy membership. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_dc_store_copy_fetch_diagnostics.py:1-16, 81-87, 148-154, 211-218` — Preserve stderr retention, check/capture compatibility, and projects-seed fetch diagnostics. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_decide_ops_seam.py:1-28, 102-107` — Preserve the public monkeypatch seam and silent-break regression guard. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_decomp_shape_criterion.py:1-11` — Preserve the deterministic decomp-shape criterion contract. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_delivered_manifest_scan_count.py:1-15, 96-100` — Preserve the invariant that delivered-child processing does not add per-child full-store scans. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_delivered_now.py:1-7` — Preserve completion-awareness semantics for delivered_now. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_delta_tree_timeout_b0e0.py:1-22` — Preserve the bounded checkout-index call in _apply_delta. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_dependency_advisory_wiring.py:1-17` — Preserve that dependency-advisory analysis is reachable from the production workflow. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_deprecation_registry.py:40-45` — Preserve the deprecation-registry compatibility behavior. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_description_cap_warning.py:1-15` — Preserve description-cap warning boundaries and non-blocking behavior. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_det_floor_clarity.py:1-17` — Preserve deterministic-floor clarity scoring. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_det_floor_operator_attested.py:1-10, 34-37` — Preserve operator-attested deterministic-floor handling. Consumer: test maintainers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_create_duplicate_warning.py tests/unit/test_criteria_overlay.py tests/unit/test_criteria_snapshot.py tests/unit/test_criteria_vocabulary_reviewers.py tests/unit/test_criterion_effectiveness.py tests/unit/test_criterion_preview.py tests/unit/test_cross_session_warn_routes.py tests/unit/test_dc_store_copy_fetch_diagnostics.py tests/unit/test_decide_ops_seam.py tests/unit/test_decomp_shape_criterion.py tests/unit/test_delivered_manifest_scan_count.py tests/unit/test_delivered_now.py tests/unit/test_delta_tree_timeout_b0e0.py tests/unit/test_dependency_advisory_wiring.py tests/unit/test_deprecation_registry.py tests/unit/test_description_cap_warning.py tests/unit/test_det_floor_clarity.py tests/unit/test_det_floor_operator_attested.py`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","id":"a0dd-88d1-a1e1-4797","parent_id":"ae4d-df34-480d-4c88","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in tests/unit — cohort 09: create_duplicate_warning–det_floor_operator_attested"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788571377145619221,"uuid":"136091cb-734e-4a88-ae0e-70865ab476fb"}